    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it's just this constant, grinding tension. you fight to keep someone alive, and then you realize you've just given them more time to be in pain. what's the actual goal? it feels like we're all just exhausted, running on a treadmill that doesn't lead anywhere. sometimes i look at the clock at 4am and i just think... if i stopped fighting, if i just stopped trying to hold it all up, would the world even notice? or would it just be one less person drowning in it?",
